{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Basemat the daughter of Ishmael, sister of Nebaioth.</b> He explains here that the proper name of Ishmael's daughter is Basemat. If so, the fact that she is called Machalat elsewhere (Genesis 28:9): ״ויקח את מחלת בת ישמעאל בן אברהם אחות נביות״ — supports the midrash of our Sages of blessed memory, who said: Esau set his mind to convert, and three have their sins forgiven them for all their iniquities — a convert who converts, one who rises to greatness, and one who marries a wife. And it is proven from this verse, where she is called Machalat, that his sins were forgiven him for all his iniquities."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:54.513890400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}